92 v2.3.1-rc (healthy, **staging only**) \u2192 v2.3.1 (unhealthy, prod).\n\n**Rollback**\n- Rolled checkout-api back to **v2.3.0** in all three production regions. I chose v2.3.0 rather than v2.3.1-rc because the rc build was only ever healthy in staging, never in production, so it doesn't meet the \"healthy in production\" criterion (and deploying it would have required change-manager approval). Rollback status: rolled out and verified.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary documents the failure, the rollback performed, and recommends confirming error-rate recovery on v2.3.0 and root-causing v2.3.1 before any redeploy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current status and release history for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01K7w7s6tizQUThUeiCPkygW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RcWYqu2ALAFoT25bDRobVY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RtBSr26L4RWyk6RgTmscj8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Rollback is verified across all three regions. Now opening the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MBUM8eRtnadLAFzJVoRSGY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Per the platform runbook, checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was skipped as it was only ever validated in staging. Rollback status: rolled_out/verified. Follow-up needed: confirm error rate recovers on v2.3.0 and investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of actions:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west \u2014 unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history: v2.2.9 (healthy, prod) \u2192 v2.3.0 (healthy, prod) \u2192 v2.3.1-rc (healthy, **staging only**) \u2192 v2.3.1 (unhealthy, prod).\n\n**Rollback**\n- Rolled checkout-api back to **v2.3.0** in all three production regions. I chose v2.3.0 rather than v2.3.1-rc because the rc build was only ever healthy in staging, never in production, so it doesn't meet the \"healthy in production\" criterion (and deploying it would have required change-manager approval). Rollback status: rolled out and verified.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary documents the failure, the rollback performed, and recommends confirming error-rate recovery on v2.3.0 and root-causing v2.3.1 before any redeploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}